# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# There was no .gitattributes here, so Git for Windows applied its default and
# checked text files out with CRLF. Five generators build their output with `\n`
# and compare it to the file on disk; all six of those comparisons failed, and
# `pnpm verify` stopped at step three on any Windows clone with:
#
#     docs/API.md is out of date. Run: pnpm docs:api
#
# Running that command rewrote an identical document, so the advice in the error
# could not work. Nothing past the third check had ever run on Windows.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` alone: `text=auto` normalises what goes into
# the repository but still hands Windows a CRLF working tree, which is the half
# that broke. Modern editors on Windows handle LF without complaint.
#
# The generators also compare newline-insensitively now (scripts/lib/generated.mjs).
# Both, deliberately — this settles what a fresh clone gets, that one keeps an
# existing checkout from reporting a difference that is not a difference.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and already-compressed formats: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs and excluded from language statistics, because
# neither is written by hand and both are large enough to bury a real change.
docs/index.html  linguist-generated=true
docs/system.html linguist-generated=true
pnpm-lock.yaml   linguist-generated=true
